Rules for declaring identifiers in Python

1. Must start with a letter (a–z, A–Z) or underscore (_)
✔️ valid: name, _value
❌ invalid: 1name
2. Cannot start with a digit
❌ 2num = 10 (wrong)
3. Can contain letters, digits, and underscores
✔️ student1, total_marks, data_2025
4. No special characters allowed
❌ total$, marks@, user-name
5. Case-sensitive
age, Age, and AGE are all different identifiers

5. Cannot use Python keywords (reserved words)
❌ if, else, for, class, True, etc.
✔️ You can check keywords using:

import keyword
print(keyword.kwlist)

